{
    "background_story": "Corbin was a majestic spider crab, a member of the esteemed Majidae family. He lived in the vibrant coral reefs of the Indo-Pacific, where his impressive leg span and vibrant coloration made him a sight to behold. Corbin was a gentle giant, often allowing smaller fish to dart in and out of his sheltering legs. He spent his days scavenging for food and protecting his territory from rival crabs. At night, Corbin would emerge from his hiding spots to perform a mesmerizing dance, waving his claws in a complex courtship ritual. His majidae heritage was evident in his regal demeanor and impressive physical prowess, earning him the respect and admiration of his fellow reef dwellers.",
